# Generated previews (level maps, wave transects, ride strips, gameplay
# screenshots) — tooling output, regenerated on demand with `make level` /
# `make waves` / `make ride` / `make screenshots`.
#
# ANCHORED to the root on purpose. Unanchored, this pattern matches a
# directory called `previews` at any depth — including a pwa/public/previews/
# the campaign menu will one day ship its banners from.
/previews/

# Recorded runs (`make record`, once it exists) — a ride is somebody's own
# measurement, not repository content.
runs/

# Release scratch
.release-notes.md

# THE PLATFORM SHELLS. `tauri/` (the desktop app) and `native/` (the store
# app) are placeholders today, each a README and nothing else. When either
# arrives it brings its own build output, its own dependency tree, its
# generated store metadata and its signing material — every one of which is
# ignored HERE, at the root, the way the sibling rally repo does it, and none
# of which may be a personal identifier or a credential in a committed file.
